# Implement the Proton Mail Bridge adapter

## Goal

Provide the supported version-one local adapter through Proton Mail Bridge
without leaking Bridge credentials or provider details into the core contract.

## Required work

- Detect and connect to an explicitly configured official Bridge installation.
- Let Bridge own Proton account login; never request the Proton password.
- Load Bridge-local credentials from an approved runtime secret source.
- Validate loopback endpoints and TLS expectations explicitly.
- Implement bounded connection pools, timeouts, cancellation, and reconnects.
- Convert provider messages and mailboxes into core domain types.
- Redact protocol diagnostics before they leave the adapter.

## Acceptance criteria

- No credential is accepted in MCP arguments or printed in diagnostics.
- Connection loss yields typed retryable errors.
- Adapter tests run against synthetic IMAP/SMTP fixtures.
- The capability domain does not depend on Bridge-specific types.
- Unsupported Gmail-parity capabilities are omitted during negotiation rather
  than simulated incorrectly or silently routed through another adapter.

## Evidence

- Adapter unit and integration tests
- Credential-leak regression tests
